+/* verify_prefetch32.c: BRAM-ring verifier/miner, AVX2 lane-parallel, with a
+ * 32-lane prefetch distance on the bank read-modify-write. Derived from the
+ * shipped champion cpu/verify_avx2.c, whose header is preserved below. The
+ * function is spec.py; this file implements it bit-exactly (make prove,
+ * host/check_vectors.py, and BRAM_EPOCH=<seed> make prove).
+ *
+ * What differs from verify_avx2.c:
+ *   - RMW scheduling: lane b's bank address a = PEXT(v_b, AMASK[b]) is known
+ *     as soon as v_b is computed, the old word bank[b][a] is consumed only on
+ *     the NEXT step (u = head XOR last_read), and every lane owns its bank.
+ *     So the read-then-write of lane b is deferred by 32 lanes: a prefetch of
+ *     &bank[b][a] is issued when lane b is computed, and the read and write
+ *     execute when lane b+32 is processed; the last 32 lanes drain at the end
+ *     of the step. Operations on distinct banks commute, including the old
+ *     word each returns, so the per-step result is unchanged.
+ *   - cell evaluation: each cell's 4-input rule is evaluated in algebraic
+ *     normal form (Boolean Mobius transform of the rule-bit masks, computed
+ *     once per epoch). spec.py admits only degree-3 rules, so 15 coefficient
+ *     masks suffice; a degree-4 coefficient aborts rather than miscomputes.
+ *   - the fill and run phases are separate loops (the fill never reads rd).
+ *   - the default benchmark times fill + run + the full SHA-256 digest for
+ *     every nonce, keeps every digest, and prints their XOR-fold after the
+ *     timer, so the digest work is observable and cannot be discarded.
+ *
+ *   cc -O3 -march=native -fopenmp -o verify_prefetch32 verify_prefetch32.c sha256.c
+ *   ./verify_prefetch32            # verify against the golden vectors + benchmark
+ *   ./verify_prefetch32 mine 0     # mine, emitting SHARE lines for race.py
+ *   ./verify_prefetch32 fold <nonce-hex> [count]   # fast fold of specific nonces
+ *   ./verify_prefetch32 vectors | python3 ../host/check_vectors.py   # the 4-column proof
+ *
+ * ---- header of the upstream champion, cpu/verify_avx2.c, as shipped ----
+ * verify_avx2.c: BRAM-ring verifier/miner, AVX2 lane-parallel. The champion
  * CPU attack: this is the number to beat if you want to close the moat from
